{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon","id":476028,"title":"Of Tribes Unspoken:Extra Tribes of the Moon?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-10T10:40:44-07:00","id":476028,"title":"Of Tribes Unspoken:Extra Tribes of the Moon?","content":"Hello all. I've got a question that I need to know, if only because not knowing is eating me up. I remember hearing in another discussion, one about the Pure(sadly I don't remember the name) in which it was mentioned a book that included three other Tribes not listed anywhere else. Sadly, I do not know what this book's name is. I apologize, but this is all I can really remember. Any help would be greatly appreciated!<br /> <br /> EDIT: I managed to remember something. One of the three favored Wisdom as their Renown and had a somewhat &quot;gnostic&quot; thematic; they were mentioned as an example of what the poster in question's idea of a Forsaken version of the Fire-Touched would look like. Hope this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3514,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","user":"ZealousChristian24","date":".  Remembered stuff 04-10-2015, 02:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:56:26-07:00","id":476091,"title":"","content":"The Pure book has the three Pure tribes, the Predator Kings, the Ivory Claws, and the Fire-touched. But they aren't Tribes of the Moon, or at least wouldn't like to be called that. The Blasphemies book offers the Bale Hounds as a Ninth Tribe, the greatest tribe.<br /> <br /> In the second edition core book, it suggests that a few new tribes could be founded. The Eaters of the Dead are seeking Ravening Wolf to form a tribe for them, and Creator Wolf may be under Basra. If excised carefully it might become a tribal totem.<br /> <br /> I don't know of any other tribes, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:01:41-07:00","id":476095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon?p=476091#post476091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure book has the three Pure tribes, the Predator Kings, the Ivory Claws, and the Fire-touched. But they aren't Tribes of the Moon, or at least wouldn't like to be called that. The Blasphemies book offers the Bale Hounds as a Ninth Tribe, the greatest tribe.<br /> <br /> In the second edition core book, it suggests that a few new tribes could be founded. The Eaters of the Dead are seeking Ravening Wolf to form a tribe for them, and Creator Wolf may be under Basra. If excised carefully it might become a tribal totem.<br /> <br /> I don't know of any other tribes, though.</div> </div> </div> </div> Er, none of those are what I meant, but thank you for trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:08:27-07:00","id":476098,"title":"","content":"There could easily be other tribes. There's more things in this world than spirits, Hosts, humans, and werewolves. Much like Vampire can have smaller Covenants there are probably smaller Tribes who aren't bonded to one of the First Born and work with lesser patrons.<br /> <br /> Infact that could be a fun campaign: encountering a hither to unknown Tribe and the conflicts that result. Hell, you could run a Silver Pack style game about the founding of a new Tribe that hunts idigam specifically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:11:09-07:00","id":476101,"title":"","content":"I don't think it would count as a Tribe without a Firstborn totem. It would just be a Lodge that's exclusive to Ghost Wolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:20:02-07:00","id":476124,"title":"","content":"In &quot;The Rage&quot; page 96-97 there are three Ghost Wolf Tribes.<br /> The Tower Hounds (Anzaghar Ilthum), the Speakers of the Vine (Khuranu Dhugu) and the Savage Priests (Idimathu)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/422-lykas","name":"Lykas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:22:06-07:00","id":476125,"title":"","content":"Oops! Ninja-ed by Lykas. GG :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":216,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","user":"Zooroos","date":".  Ninja-ed! 04-10-2015, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:22:33-07:00","id":476126,"title":"","content":"Wow, there you go.<br /> <br /> Stupid Ghost Wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:36:10-07:00","id":476139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lykas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon?p=476124#post476124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In &amp;quot;The Rage&amp;quot; page 96-97 there are three Ghost Wolf Tribes.<br /> The Tower Hounds (Anzaghar Ilthum), the Speakers of the Vine (Khuranu Dhugu) and the Savage Priests (Idimathu)</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank you! And thanks to everyone else for trying to help. Thank you all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T11:58:18-07:00","id":476181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon?p=476091#post476091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Pure book has the three Pure tribes, the Predator Kings, the Ivory Claws, and the Fire-touched. But they aren't Tribes of the Moon, or at least wouldn't like to be called that. The Blasphemies book offers the Bale Hounds as a Ninth Tribe, the greatest tribe.<br /> <br /> In the second edition core book, it suggests that a few new tribes could be founded. The Eaters of the Dead are seeking Ravening Wolf to form a tribe for them, and Creator Wolf may be under Basra. If excised carefully it might become a tribal totem.<br /> <br /> I don't know of any other tribes, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know of the Bales Hounds being the GREATEST tribe, I would politely like to submit the Fire-Touched for that title XD<br /> <br /> I actually am using Danu-Ur for a fourth Pure Tribe Totem in my 2nd ed campaign, completely revamping a Pure Tribe I created for 1st ed.<br /> <br /> There are also the possibilities of the Ghost Wolves creating Tribes such as the Tower Hounds of the Savage Priests, which are secret police and a forsaken version of the Fire-Touched ( though I might wrong about the Tower Hounds.. I think the Savage Priests double as secret police). There was a third potential Ghost Wolf Tribe.. but I forget it's name XD<br /> (( thanks for reminding me of the Speakers of the Vine, Lykas.. total brain spasm on my part XD))<br /> <br /> oh, there is also the &quot;Tribe&quot; created by the Deceiver Lune, the Urdam","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-10-2015, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T12:01:04-07:00","id":476184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon?p=476101#post476101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it would count as a Tribe without a Firstborn totem. It would just be a Lodge that's exclusive to Ghost Wolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing says the Firstborn are required to be the patron of a Tribe, though they became so for the eight tribes. I believe any spirit of similar power could also act as the totem for such huge numbers of Uratha - the nine separate sects of Bale Hounds are more like tribes than lodges","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-10-2015, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T05:21:44-07:00","id":478967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon?p=476184#post476184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nothing says the Firstborn are required to be the patron of a Tribe, though they became so for the eight tribes. I believe any spirit of similar power could also act as the totem for such huge numbers of Uratha - the nine separate sects of Bale Hounds are more like tribes than lodges</div> </div> </div> </div>Not arguing. But.<br /> <br /> How about some suggestions as to spirits that might rival the Firstborn in power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T05:28:45-07:00","id":478969,"title":"","content":"Spirits of the sky or widespread phenomena or animals. Nature, money, military, certain belief systems not just religious. Many countries. Concepts like war, peace, crime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T20:20:00-07:00","id":479811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gebbethine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon?p=478967#post478967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not arguing. But.<br /> <br /> How about some suggestions as to spirits that might rival the Firstborn in power?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maeljin, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T20:50:02-07:00","id":479849,"title":"","content":"Hmm, aren't the first born rank 6 or 7 according to werewolf second edition, or are they only rank 7?<br /> <br /> If rank 6, then god like spirits of &quot;planet wide phenomena&quot; qualify- nations, oceans, thunder, and drought are all examples from Imperial mysteries.<br /> <br /> At rank 7, there are spirits of entire species would count, although I imagine the number who would be willing to support a tribe would be rather limited there I would think.<br /> <br /> I mean sure, Polar Bear has the mojo to support a tribe, but if he was interested, why would he invest in adopted children when he could support his own?<br /> <br /> This coming from the section of godlike spirits from Imperial mysteries, which as a first edition book might be subject to retcons when it gets talked about in second edition.<br /> <br /> Although that gives me an idea for an interesting lodge- A group of ghost wolves who decided that they wanted no part in uratha culture, but like a local non-uratha shapeshifter types. The adopted children of bear, or panther. I can't imagine the local uratha of the tribes being too thrilled there...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 04-13-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T22:02:58-07:00","id":479898,"title":"","content":"The Firstborn are rank 7, Ilusah. 'Ilusahim are the aloof and distant gods of Shadow - spirits of global or universal phenomena, and rulers of entire umia. The 'weaker' Ilusah are spirits like the Firstborn; patrons of entire tribes. Mother Luna and her brother Helios are the best known greater Ilusahim.'<br /> <br /> I think 7 would be more like Bear, or Spider, with 6 being more specific ones like Polar Bear and Tarantula. The Firstborn seem to get a big boost from being Father Wolf's children, and are not 'merely' spirits of wolves. Fenris-Ur, for instance, is pretty clearly a spirit of destruction.<br /> <br /> The Maeljin seem to have gotten a downgrade to Diharim, which seems to be rank 6, but the way its described suggests they may be more than our old, familiar 9.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-14-2015, 01:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T22:28:23-07:00","id":479915,"title":"","content":"Like the cenobites the maeljin change! And they have such sights to show you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-13T22:42:02-07:00","id":479941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/476028-of-tribes-unspoken-extra-tribes-of-the-moon?p=479898#post479898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Maeljin seem to have gotten a downgrade to Diharim, which seems to be rank 6, but the way its described suggests they may be more than our old, familiar 9.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mind, the notion that there are nine Maeljin was itself called out as possibly erroneous right out the gate in the 1e core sidebar that first named them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T02:31:06-07:00","id":480026,"title":"","content":"Oh I see, I remembered the bit about the first born being lesser ilusahi, and forgot which ranks that world corresponds with.<br /> <br /> I'm not as good at vocabulary words as I used to be. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}